  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z=-1 \\\\ x-y+3z=2 \\\\ -2x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9$ is unique, and the inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe solution of the system of equations is \n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}, \n$\\,z=$\n{{field-3}}.",
